  <Control id="Lbl-LamText" type="Label" x="48" y="160" w="1024" h="96" tab-order="0" z-order="0" visible="true" enabled="true" parent="Tab-Main" tab="4">
    <Property name="Caption">PowerCloud never signs a download link itself. The function powercloud-presign does: given the key of one photo, it answers a link to that object that works for 15 minutes, signed with a role that can only read the photo bucket. Use it to hand a photo to someone outside the application, in a browser or an e-mail. The application itself reads its photos through AWS&apos;s MCP server, as it makes every other AWS call; it never fetches the bytes behind a link. AwsLambda.Invoke needs AllowWrite on, because a function can do whatever its code says.</Property>
